  "result": "Perfect! All 137 tests pass. Added date utility functions that work in UTC.\n\n**New file src/dates.js:**\n\n1. **`isValidDate(text)`** \u2014 Validates YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - Checks format pattern\n   - Verifies it's a real date (catches Feb 30, etc.)\n   - Returns boolean\n\n2. **`addDays(date, n)`** \u2014 Adds n days to a date (UTC)\n   - Positive n adds days forward\n   - Negative n subtracts days\n   - Crosses month/year boundaries correctly\n   - Returns YYYY-MM-DD string\n\n3. **`daysBetween(a, b)`** \u2014 Days between two dates (b minus a)\n   - Positive result if b is after a\n   - Negative result if b is before a\n   - Returns whole days (no fractions)\n   - Returns number\n\n**Updated src/invoices.js:**\n- Replaced inline date validation with `isValidDate(issueDate)` call\n- Cleaner, more testable code\n\n**Tests added (31 date tests):**\n- \u2713 Valid dates (including edge cases)\n- \u2713 Invalid formats (slashes, reversed order, incomplete)\n- \u2713 Invalid actual dates (Feb 30, month 13)\n- \u2713 Leap year handling (2024 vs 2026)\n- \u2713 Date arithmetic (positive/negative, boundaries)\n- \u2713 UTC consistency\n- \u2713 Inverse relationship (addDays and daysBetween)\n\nKey behavior:\n- All dates work in UTC (no local timezone issues)\n- Invalid dates properly rejected (not just format checking)\n- Date arithmetic is consistent and reversible\n- createInvoice now uses proper date validation\n\nAll 137 tests pass.",
